<http://dbpedia.org/property/itWasTheEndOfTheGreatDepression;CanadaHadRecentlyEnteredWorldWarIi;AndVancouverStillBoreTheScarsOfTheTumultuous1930s.AfterTheStockMarketCrashOf1929,AttractedByVancouver’sTemperateClimate,HordesOfCanadiansHadFlockedToTheCityOnlyToFindLittleWorkAndEndUpSettlingInMakeshiftShantytownsAnd%22hoboJungles%22.TheEnactmentOfTheUnemploymentInsuranceActIn1940AndABuoyedEconomyHelpedTemperSomeOfTheDesperation,ButManyMenWereStillCaughtInTheCycleOfPovertyAndHomelessness,AndAlcoholismWasWidespread.BobStaceyHadWitnessedTheManySuccessesGodWasCreatingThroughTheRescueMissionInNycAndFeltCalledToHelpTheStrugglingMenAndVancouver.HeRaised$1,000InStartUpCostsByGettingTheWordOutOnReverendArnoldBennett’sDailyRadioProgram,MorningDevotions.HeRecruitedVolunteersWhoWantedToServeThePoor,HadSuppliesDonatedByLocalChurches,AndSecuredRentForTheUpstairsOf10PowellStreetAt$25AMonth.TheFacilityCouldSeat60People,HadASmallKitchenAndSixBedsForMenToStayTheNight.EveryEvening,Bob,AlongsideChurchGroups,Choirs,AndOtherVolunteers,WouldOfferAChapelServiceWithSoupAndASandwichServedToGuestsAfterward.UgmWasOpenEveryDay,AndBobWouldReachOutToThoseInNeedInTheNeighbourhoodAndGiveHelpToAllWhoAsked.DuringTheDay,AUgmVehicleWouldPickUpDonatedFoodFromWoodward’sFoodDepartmentDowntown,AsWellAsOtherLocalBakeries.OnDecember25th,1940,UgmHeldItsFirstEverChristmasDinnerForTheCommunityAndServedOver100People.Today,UgmServesOver3500MealsAtItsAnnualChristmasDinner,AndOver260,000MealsAnnually.We’veExpandedOurProgramsAndServicesSignificantlyAndGrownToFill9LocationsThroughoutMetroVancouverAndTheCityOfMission.It’sTakenVisionaryLeadershipAndStrongFaithInGod’sProvisionToBringUgmToWhereItIsToday.GodIsAlwaysAtTheHelmOfUgm,ButHereAreTheMenWhoseSuperiorLeadershipHasHelpedGuideTheOrganizationToWhereItIsTodayGordon(bob)R.Stacey1940–1943LeonardKlassen1943–1980MauriceMcelrea1980–2008WilliamB.Mollard2008–PresentCompanyName> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
